  "entries": [
    {
      "title": "The autumn tide times are up by the door",
      "slug": "autumn-tide-times",
      "values": {
        "summary": "The table for October to December is pinned by the hut door, every swim we keep marked in orange.",
        "image": {
          "mediaId": "tide-window",
          "alt": "Two days of tide in the bay: the water rising and falling, slack water marked in red at every turn, and in orange the two swims, at the slack that falls at first light"
        },
        "body": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "We still post the week’s times here and by the hut door every Friday. The whole autumn is up now too, so you can plan your mornings ahead."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Slack water comes about fifty minutes later each day. When the morning slack falls before first light, we swim at the next one instead."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The times are a guide, not a promise: wind and pressure move the water too. If the bay looks wrong on the day, we stay out."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "date": "2026-09-26"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Bright caps for the dark mornings",
      "slug": "bright-caps",
      "values": {
        "summary": "The dawn swims start in half light now. Wear a bright cap, so the boat and the shore can count every head.",
        "image": {
          "mediaId": "g-caps",
          "alt": "Three swim caps, orange, pink and white, at the waterline"
        },
        "body": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "From October the sun comes up after we get in. An orange or a pink cap shows on grey water; a black or a navy one does not."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "If you have no bright cap, there is a box of club caps in the hut. Take one, and keep it."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "date": "2026-10-01"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Tea in the hut on Sundays",
      "slug": "tea-in-the-hut",
      "values": {
        "summary": "Through the winter series the hut by the slipway opens after every Sunday swim: a kettle, a heater and the big red flask.",
        "image": {
          "mediaId": "m-tea",
          "alt": "A red flask and two enamel mugs of tea on a rock after a swim"
        },
        "body": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Warming up is half of a winter swim. From 1 November the hut opens after every Sunday swim, so nobody changes on the slipway in the wind."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Members take turns with the kettle. The list is on the hut door: put your name down for one Sunday in the season."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The tea is free. Biscuits come with whoever remembers them."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "date": "2026-10-04"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "A rockpool morning for children",
      "slug": "rockpool-morning",
      "values": {
        "summary": "On Saturday 24 October, at low water, we take children along the rocks at the north end to see what the tide leaves behind.",
        "image": {
          "mediaId": "g-rockpools",
          "alt": "Rock pools at low water, kelp at their edges and a starfish in one"
        },
        "body": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The tide goes out a long way that morning, and the pools under the north rocks fill with crabs, anemones and, if we are lucky, a starfish."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Children come with a grown-up. Wear shoes that can get wet, and something warm. We look, we count, and we put everything back where we found it."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Meet at the slipway at ten. No swimming that day: just looking."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "date": "2026-10-10"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "The winter series starts on 1 November",
      "slug": "winter-series-starts",
      "values": {
        "summary": "Short, cold swims every Sunday from 1 November to the end of March, and very hot tea after every one.",
        "image": {
          "mediaId": "m-winter",
          "alt": "The jetty in winter, the safe-water mark beyond it"
        },
        "body": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The first winter swim is on Sunday 1 November. We meet at the north slipway twenty minutes before slack water, as we always do, and the time goes up by the hut door on the Friday before."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Each swim is one loop of the buoys, ten minutes at most, in groups of four with a coach in the boat. If you have swum with us through the autumn, you are ready for it."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "What to bring, and what a Sunday costs, is on the "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "winter series page",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "/winter-series"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "date": "2026-10-14"
      }
    }
  ],
